WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.790
25 April 2015, Nepal: a
magnitude 7.8 earthquake,

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.330
by USGS's measure.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:14.530
14 November 2016, Kaikōura, New
Zealand: also magnitude 7.8.

4
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.610
Both set off huge numbers of
landslides: at least 25,000 in Nepal,

5
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.350
and over 10,000 at Kaikōura.

6
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.930
In Nepal, more than 8,790 people died.

7
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.530
At Kaikōura, 2 people died.

8
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.670
Was Nepal's earthquake
really much stronger?

9
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.130
Was it pure luck?

10
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.870
Why such a difference?

11
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.350
In this mission, you'll build
a profile of each earthquake:

12
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.930
plates, faults, depth
and secondary hazards.

13
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.090
Then you'll trace the impacts on
people's well-being and recovery,

14
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.050
and compare the two side by side.

15
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:54.010
Your mission: explain why two earthquakes
of the same magnitude had such different

16
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.070
death tolls.
